# 📘 DBMS Quick Revision Notes

## 🔹 Data vs Information
- Data → Raw facts (numbers, text)
- Information → Processed, meaningful data

---

## 🔹 Types of Data
- Structured → Tables (SQL)
- Unstructured → Images, videos
- Semi-structured → JSON, XML

---

## 🔹 Database
- Organized collection of data stored electronically

---

## 🔹 DBMS (Database Management System)
- Software to store, retrieve, and manage data

Examples: MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle

---

## 🔹 Components of DBMS
- Hardware
- Software
- Data
- Procedures
- Users
- Database Access Language

---

## 🔹 View of Data (3 Levels)
1. Physical Level → How data is stored
2. Logical Level → What data is stored
3. View Level → User-specific view

---

## 🔹 Data Abstraction
- Hides complexity of data
- Levels: Physical → Logical → View

---

## 🔹 Instance vs Schema
- Instance → Current data in database (changes frequently)
- Schema → Structure/design of database (rarely changes)

---

## 🔹 Data Models
- Hierarchical Model
- Network Model
- Relational Model
- ER Model

---

## 🔹 Database Languages
- DDL → CREATE, ALTER, DROP
- DML → INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE
- DCL → GRANT, REVOKE

---

## 🔹 Applications of DBMS
- Banking
- E-commerce
- Airlines
- Education
- Healthcare

---

## 🔹 ER Model (Entity-Relationship Model)
- Entity → Object (Student, Employee)
- Attribute → Property (Name, Age)
- Relationship → Connection between entities

---

## 🔹 DBMS Architecture
- 1-tier → Direct database access
- 2-tier → Client–Server
- 3-tier → Client → Application → Database

---

## ⚡ Summary
DBMS helps in efficient storage, retrieval, and management of data using abstraction and structured models.
